{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","title":"def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2626,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:scalar-product-signature-form]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:sylvesters-law-inertia]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","line":4434,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Signature of a Pseudo-Riemannian Metric at a Point]\n\\label{def:pseudo-metric-signature-at}\n\n\\uses{def:pseudo-riemannian-metric, lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product, cor:scalar-product-signature-form, prop:sylvesters-law-inertia}\n\n\n\n\nFor a pseudo-Riemannian manifold $(M,g)$ and $p\\in M$, let $(r_p,s_p)$ be the\nsignature of the scalar product $(T_pM,g_p)$. This is the \\emph{signature of $g$\nat $p$}, and $s_p$ is its \\emph{index}. Equivalently, $r_p$ and $s_p$ are the\nmaximal dimensions of subspaces on which $g_p$ is respectively positive and\nnegative definite.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Signature of a Pseudo-Riemannian Metric at a Point] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a70736575646f2d6d65747269632d7369676e61747572652d6174\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aps